.TH QUARTERDECK 1 "August 2026" "quarterdeck 0.12.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quarterdeck \- local orchestration board for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quarterdeck
.RI [ --host " " ip ]
.RI [ --port " " number|auto ]
.RI [ --no-open ]
.RI [ --no-native-ui ]
.RI [ --skip-shutdown-cleanup ]
.br
.B quarterdeck hooks
.RI " " ingest|notify
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck statusline
.br
.B quarterdeck backup
.RI " " create|list|restore
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck diagnostics
.RI " " list|status|doctor|capture|watch|record|mark
.RI " " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quarterdeck
starts the local Quarterdeck runtime and serves the web UI. When launched inside a Git repository, it opens that repository's indexed workspace. When launched outside Git, it starts without an active workspace or uses an indexed project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --host <ip>
Bind the runtime to an IP address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --port <number|auto>
Bind to a port from 1 through 65535, or select an available port automatically.
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B --no-native-ui
Disable integrations that launch or interact with host-native UI.
.TP
.B --skip-shutdown-cleanup
Skip graceful shutdown cleanup, including session marking and orphan-process cleanup. Intended for controlled testing and recovery only.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hooks ingest [payload]
Ingest an agent hook event into a running Quarterdeck instance. The payload may be supplied as an argument or on standard input. Hook adapters can also provide structured fields with options including
.BR --source ,
.BR --activity-text ,
.BR --tool-name ,
.BR --tool-input-summary ,
.BR --final-message ,
.BR --hook-event-name ,
.BR --notification-type ,
.BR --session-id ,
.BR --session-instance-id ,
.BR --turn-id ,
.BR --tool-use-id ,
.BR --transcript-path ,
and
.BR --metadata-base64 .
.TP
.B hooks notify [payload]
Best-effort variant of
.BR "hooks ingest" .
It accepts the same hook fields and does not fail the calling agent when delivery is unavailable.
.TP
.B statusline
Read Claude Code status JSON from standard input and render the Quarterdeck statusline.
.TP
.B backup create
Create a manual snapshot of Quarterdeck state.
.TP
.B backup list
List available state backups.
.TP
.B backup restore [backup]
Restore a named backup directory, an explicit backup path, or the most recent backup when omitted. The Quarterdeck server must not be running.
.TP
.B diagnostics list
List active and recently retained runtime instances.
.TP
.B diagnostics status
Show recorder and journal health for a selected runtime.
.TP
.B diagnostics doctor
Run read-only subsystem checks. Use
.B --request-browser
to request a fresh metadata-only browser snapshot and
.B --fail-on-error
to return exit status 5 when an error-severity finding exists.
.TP
.B diagnostics capture
Write a canonical local bundle containing the correlated JSONL timeline, findings, bounded snapshots, and a hashed manifest. Use
.B --output
to select a new output directory.
.TP
.B diagnostics watch
Watch bounded records for a limited duration. Use
.B --jsonl
for one JSON object per line.
.TP
.B diagnostics record
Start, inspect, or stop an automatically expiring deep-recording window. Recording can be scoped by project, task, and category and is capped at 15 minutes.
.TP
.B diagnostics mark <message>
Add a bounded correlation marker to the diagnostic timeline.
.PP
Diagnostic selection commands accept options for a specific runtime instance and scoped project, task, session, operation, source, level, event, and time range. Use each subcommand's
.B --help
for the complete option set.
.PP
The lightweight metadata-only flight recorder starts automatically. Deep recording remains content-safe and does not enable terminal transcripts or Git diffs. Bundles are private local directories and are never uploaded automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the runtime on the default loopback address:
.B quarterdeck
.TP
Start without browser or host-native integrations:
.B quarterdeck --no-open --no-native-ui
.TP
Bind to a custom address and port:
.B quarterdeck --host 0.0.0.0 --port 9000
.TP
Create and list state backups:
.B quarterdeck backup create
.br
.B quarterdeck backup list
.TP
Capture current diagnostic evidence:
.B quarterdeck diagnostics capture --request-browser
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Command or runtime operation failed.
.TP
.B 5
.B diagnostics doctor --fail-on-error
found an error-severity issue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR npm (1)
